      <h2>2. AI-Generated Content and Output Accuracy</h2>
      <div class="legal-alert amber"><p><strong>AI outputs are probabilistic by nature.</strong> They may be plausible, well-formatted, and confident in tone — and still be factually wrong, incomplete, outdated, or entirely fabricated. Agentivity does not generate these outputs and has no control over them.</p></div>
      <p>The AI agents you build on Agentivity connect to large language models (LLMs) of your choice, operated by third-party providers under their own terms. LLMs generate text by predicting statistically likely sequences of tokens based on training data. This process is fundamentally different from a deterministic lookup or a verified database query. As a result:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Outputs may contain <strong>factual errors</strong>, including incorrect dates, figures, names, citations, or statements of law or science.</li>
        <li>Outputs may contain <strong>hallucinations</strong> — plausible-sounding but entirely fabricated information that has no basis in fact.</li>
        <li>Outputs may be <strong>outdated</strong>, as LLM training data has a knowledge cutoff date.</li>
        <li>Outputs may be <strong>biased</strong> in ways that reflect the biases present in the training data.</li>
        <li>Outputs may vary significantly between identical or similar inputs (non-deterministic behaviour).</li>
        <li>Outputs may be inappropriate, offensive, or unsuitable for your specific business context.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Agentivity makes <strong>no representations or warranties</strong> regarding the accuracy, completeness, reliability, suitability, or fitness for purpose of any output generated by any AI agent configured on the Platform, regardless of how that agent is configured.</p>
      <p><strong>You are solely responsible</strong> for reviewing, validating, and taking responsibility for any AI-generated output before acting upon it, sharing it with third parties, publishing it, or using it to make any decision.</p>
